{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1107677-1001-changeling-plots","id":1107677,"title":"1001 changeling plots","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-25T10:26:15-07:00","id":1107677,"title":"1001 changeling plots","content":"We need to start one of these for C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T00:08:28-07:00","id":1108311,"title":"","content":"A man is walking down the Champs-Elys\u00e9es in Paris. It's night and cars try to avoid him, sending manic beams of light in the night. The man acts insane, looks like a tramp, and walks as if he's drunk. Police cars sirens are echoing and rapidly approaching. In fact, this man is in the throes of his Dream-Dance. He experiences flashes of prophetic scenes as well as visions of Arcadia assaulted by Nightmarish forces, spawning ephemeral chimera around him, some of them being Wyrd, which throw the drivers of the cars into more disarray. Soon, there is a huge traffic jam on the famous avenue. The man, totally lost in his dream-world, doesn't notice the cops who are approaching on foot. He is looking to the west, toward the Arc de Triomphe, the Arche de la D\u00e9fense and, further, toward the Seine River, even toward the Channel Sea -- toward Arcadia. What he's seeing is the greatest trod in Western Europe, the Trod of Dragons, opened before his feet. He also sees a sea-god emerging from the waves in the crushing sound of the sea on the beach under the moonlight. He recognizes the sea-god, and starts to address him in Breton:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hail to thee, Lord--&quot;<br /> <br /> Then, all becomes black as the club of the cop cracks open his skull.<br /> <br /> Later, bloody, with cranial trauma, the trump wakes up in a police cell. His sight is blurry, and one of his eyes is blinded by dried blood. He croaks a plaintive groan. He can hear a voice calling for help over a phone. He can also hear the cries and screams of those who are detained. Then, suddenly, almost unconsciously, the man senses fear. A deep, primordial fear that grows up in him as he perceives a coldness coming closer. His new senses can almost make out the figure who is descending the stairs toward the cells room -- Dauntain.<br /> <br /> Outside, several Kithain have gathered and they can perceive both the lingering traces of Glamour -- the same one as the Chrysalis they sensed before -- and the dread cold of Banality.<br /> <br /> There is no time to loose.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> [Note: the tramp as well as the rescuing changelings are PCs.]<br /> <br /> [Note 2: music <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HSiEoS7ga3c\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You Will Rise&quot; by Tom McRae</a>.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:09:05-07:00","id":1108506,"title":"","content":"2-EAT, DRINK AND BE MERRY, FOR TOMORROW... The characters are invited to the party of the year. During the revelry the heir to a nearby freehold is brutally murdered, and all evidence points to the PCs. Do they have an enemy setting them up? Does the heir have an enemy looking for a patsy to blame? Is the Shadow Court trying to destabilize local politics? Did one of the characters actually do it under some form of mind control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:12:51-07:00","id":1109592,"title":"","content":"Assuming the PCs live near water:<br /> <br /> The PCs are watching TV when they see coverage of a naked man found wandering on the beach. He appears to be injured or perhaps mal-formed the blood occludes that, however he is screaming about his people needing help. The Kraken have begun to stir and the first of them, the weakest of them has begun to attack his people. He screams all this as men carrying a white coat and butterfly nets chase him around the beach (too much TV I know : )<br /> <br /> This might all be dismissed if, as he is finally caught he did not shout, &quot;I call on you Cousins who walk the Land, by Salt, by Moon, and by Tide. On Oaths sworn to render aid. I call on you find me.&quot;<br /> <br /> And damn if at that very moment the Dreaming didn't just slap the PC in the face and let him know that he, or a liege-lord in his past bound him in to an oath that is being called upon today.<br /> <br /> Note: This puts the players in a timed situation. It's hard to imagine a more Nightmarish or Banal place than a Mental Hospital. If they don't get to the Merman soon he may never be able to lead them back to where his people need help...<br /> <br /> Add to the tension the fact that whatever oath binds the PC or PCs now may have more strings attached. &quot;Well of course you dealt with the Kraken pup and we thank you, but having accepted the Quest you MUST see it through by the Old Oaths... go find and kill Mama,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T22:11:56-07:00","id":1109625,"title":"","content":"A slight twist on Yrtalien's Mer story...<br /> <br /> IDEA 1:<br /> The Mer grow sick and tired of stupid mud-walkers dumping their pollutants and Coldness (Banality) into their beloved Mother Ocean. Logical solution? War!<br /> So how do you fight stupid humans when their very presence makes you drown in Mother Ocean? Skycraft from afar, of course. So the mer start a series of storms and tidal waves that will hit on the PCs hometown. The big Tsunami is soon to come, but maybe the characters can intervene?<br /> <br /> IDEA 2:<br /> If war stories are not to your liking, and you want court intrigue and investigation... It's been a year since the war with the Mer, and the Court of the character's hometown and the Underwater kingdom that was fighting them will sign a Peace accord. So, the Mer's Queen deigns come to land to talk to the hometown's Duke. As token of good will, her guards bring along a treasure chest, within which there lies the Eye of the Ocean, an amulet of enormous magical power. As a counter token, the Duke brings an enchanted sword, as beautiful and resplendent as it is deadly. They place the Treasures together in sight of all changelings and swear an Oath on their power to honor the truce. They head back to negociate while mer delegates get to mingle with land-dwellers. The Queen and Duke decide on a hostage exchange: The beautiful mermaid princess will stay on land for a year and a day, while the Duke's kinain son will go to the Depths for the same amount of time. However, as they are deciding on this, someone steals the treasures. Can the characters find the treasures before the Queen realizes they are missing? Will war restart over this? And why were they stolen, in the first place?<br /> <br /> Tune in for the answer to these questions, same Changeling channel, same Changeling time...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T08:51:24-07:00","id":1111282,"title":"","content":"Duke Fancypants has been arrested for acting like a loon in public (again) and you're the only one who knows this. Do you go rescue him in order to score political points or do you leave him so that his son (who is much less of a jerk, and who may or may not be your boyfriend) takes the throne (or so that you can lead a commoner rebellion against the nobles, depending on your allegiance)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}